1.0.1 2026-07-17
  - Page setup for Scientific Data review: HowToAcknowledge cites OpenNeuro accession/DOI; ReferencesAndLinks add public code repo + BIDS/MNE-BIDS citations.
  - Search metadata completed (domain, design, modalities eeg/beh, tasks, trial count, healthy controls, cross-sectional).
  - Private draft retained; not published. Reviewer link available separately.
1.22.0 2026-07-16
 - beh/*_physio.json: removed the "Levels" object from the shot_target column (all 20
   files). shot_target is a continuous 100 Hz recording stored as floats, so a categorical
   Levels enumeration (integer keys "0"-"4") mis-declared the column type and failed BIDS
   validation (TSV_VALUE_INCORRECT_TYPE). It is now a plain numeric column with Units +
   Description -- matching the sibling shot_confirm column -- with the five code meanings
   (0 = miss; 1-3 = active-condition colour AA/SA/F; 4 = white "Bait") retained in full in
   the Description. No data changed; build_physio COL_META synced.

1.21.0 2026-07-16
 - dataset_description.json: License set to "CC0-1.0" (public-domain dedication;
   the Scientific Data norm for the dataset and required for the planned OpenNeuro
   deposit). Added a top-level LICENSE file with the full CC0 1.0 Universal legalcode.
 - dataset_description.json: Authors updated to the final 10-author list and order
   (added Brian Morrissey and Alexander Michael Hoelken). CONTRIBUTIONS.md synced;
   CRediT roles for the two added authors are pending confirmation.
 - README: montage/electrode documentation made explicit for reviewers. Electrode
   positions were not digitised, so no electrodes.tsv/coordsystem.json are included;
   the layout is the standard extended-10/10 cap template. Cross-checked against the
   manufacturer cap document (EASYCAP "Standard 64Ch actiCAP snap", order code CACS-64,
   REF FCz / GND Fpz): all 64 channel names and their order match the published layout
   exactly, and also match MNE's easycap-M1 template and the lab's chanlocs.mat.
   Corrected a stale README "extended 10/20" mention to "10/10".

1.20.0 2026-07-16
 - Condition terminology aligned with the manuscript (Eric Loh feedback). The
   trial_type value "synchronous" was renamed to "simultaneous" across all 20
   events.tsv (data value), task-duorhythm_events.json (trial_type Levels key +
   description), 2_build_events / 5_verify_bids, and the IBS analysis
   (ibs_analysis_full + result CSVs). Trial balance unchanged (30/30/30 = 90;
   event-count check re-run, still PASSED).
 - Descriptions now name the "alternating action" (AA) and "simultaneous action"
   (SA) conditions to match the paper, in the shot_target and trial_type
   descriptions/Levels of task-duorhythm_events.json and the 20 beh/*_physio.json
   (build_events + build_physio COL_META synced). Dropped the article: "the white
   'Bait' distractor" -> "white 'Bait' distractor".
 - beh/*_physio.json units spelled out for the sidecar: crosshair_x/_y Units
   "arbitrary (Unity 2D world units)" -> "arbitrary units (a.u.)"; crosshair_vx/_vy
   -> "arbitrary units per second (a.u./s)"; shot_confirm/shot_target/score ->
   "arbitrary units (a.u.)". The "Unity 2D world" detail remains in each Description.
   build_physio COL_META synced. Sidecar text only; the physio .tsv.gz are unchanged.

1.19.0 2026-07-15
 - beh/*_physio.json: expanded the "score" description to state the direction and
   dynamics -- higher is better; the shared block score rises on correct coloured-target
   hits and falls on white "Bait" hits; the task goal is to maximise it. Description text
   only across the 20 sidecars; data unchanged. build_physio COL_META updated to match.

1.18.0 2026-07-15
 - Sidecar description text synced to the build notebooks (no data changed; a fresh
   1->4 rebuild reproduces these). Changes vs the previous build:
   * eeg.json EEGPlacementScheme is "based on the extended 10/10 system (EasyCap M1
     layout)" -- the accurate descriptor for the 64-channel easycap-M1 layout
     (supersedes the "extended 10/20 system" wording noted under 1.12.0).
   * task-duorhythm_events.json "value": simplified to "Raw trial-type trigger code
     (XY: X=condition 1/2/3, Y=1 start). n/a for button presses." -- dropped the
     pre-conversion source-channel reference, which could confuse readers unfamiliar
     with the raw XDF behavioural channel layout.
   * eeg.json InstitutionName given in full ("... Graduate University"); participants.json
     "pair" and the shot_target descriptions (events.json + the 20 physio.json) lightly
     reworded. Levels/values and all data unchanged.

1.17.0 2026-07-15
 - Dataset name styling normalised to "Duorhythm" (was "DuoRhythm") in
   dataset_description.json (Name) and the README title. The lowercase BIDS task label
   (task-duorhythm) is unchanged.
 - phenotype/*.json: removed the source questionnaire filename ("06. Questionnaire_ENG
   2024.07.31") from the four MeasurementToolMetadata descriptions -- that file is not
   distributed with the dataset, and each sidecar already carries the full item wording,
   so the reference was a dead pointer. Now reads "From the Duorhythm questionnaire."
   README questionnaire section updated to match. Description text only; data unchanged.
 - dataset_description.json: fixed the stale GeneratedBy entry (convert_to_bids.ipynb ->
   1_eeg_to_bids.ipynb, matching the pipeline rename).

1.16.0 2026-07-15
 - beh/*_physio.json: documented the crosshair units. crosshair_x/_y are the game's
   2D Unity world coordinates (origin-centred floats; per Eric Loh's thesis appendix,
   the game is built in Unity 2022.3.10f1 and blocks reset the crosshairs to (-0.5, 0)
   and (0.5, 0)); crosshair_vx/_vy are their per-second time-derivatives (verified:
   velocity = d(position)/dt at the 100 Hz rate, correlation ~1.0). Units changed from
   "arbitrary" to "arbitrary (Unity 2D world units)" and "... per second"; descriptions
   expanded. Description/Units text only -- the physio data (.tsv.gz) are unchanged.
   README updated. build_physio COL_META updated to match.

1.15.0 2026-07-15
 - phenotype: restored the two pre-experiment subscales (display_comfort = Part 2,
   game_familiarity = Part 3) for sub-02, sub-04, sub-10 and sub-20. These four P2
   surveys recorded only the pre-experiment half; those Likert values were present in
   the source but had previously been withheld as n/a. Their post-experiment subscales
   (coordination_skill, coordination_level) remain n/a, flagged in KnownIssues (Parts
   4-5 not recorded). Confirmed by Eric Loh. build_phenotype + README updated.

1.14.0 2026-07-15
 - Streamlined the shot_target descriptions in task-duorhythm_events.json and the 20
